WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.560
There's a lot going on in the new trailer
for Spider-Man: Far From Home, including one

00:00:04.560 --> 00:00:08.220
big reveal about the state of the MCU in the
wake of Avengers: Endgame.

00:00:08.220 --> 00:00:12.100
But with an illusionist like Mysterio in the
mix, all might not be as it appears.

00:00:12.100 --> 00:00:15.600
Now that we've seen the new trailer, here
are some small details you may have missed.

00:00:15.600 --> 00:00:19.140
And by the way, big spoilers for Endgame ahead,
you've been warned.

00:00:19.340 --> 00:00:23.420
For a brief moment in the trailer, we see
Peter Parker rocking a very familiar looking

00:00:23.440 --> 00:00:24.560
pair of sunglasses.

00:00:24.560 --> 00:00:27.380
That's right: those are Tony Stark's signature
shades.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:30.949
While it's not very clear what he's doing
with them, he seems to have a pretty shocked

00:00:30.949 --> 00:00:33.160
expression on his face after looking through
them.

00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:36.590
That may have something to do with the fact
that those sunglasses are a bit more than

00:00:36.590 --> 00:00:40.520
a gift from a fallen friend: they're probably
filled with Stark's signature nano-tech.

00:00:40.520 --> 00:00:45.040
In Avengers: Infinity War, we see Stark put
those glasses on shortly after Cull Obsidian

00:00:45.040 --> 00:00:46.580
and Ebony Maw appear on Earth.

00:00:46.580 --> 00:00:50.820
When he does, he starts talking to his AI
assistant, Friday, which seems to indicate

00:00:50.820 --> 00:00:55.040
that they provide a direct link to Stark technology
even without wearing an Iron Man suit.

00:00:55.040 --> 00:00:59.320
Shortly afterward, when Stark activates his
nano-tech to turn into Iron Man, he takes

00:00:59.320 --> 00:01:02.440
off his glasses, and they seem to actually
disappear in his hand.

00:01:02.440 --> 00:01:06.720
So are the glasses an advanced piece of Stark
nano-technology that helps Peter in his fight

00:01:06.720 --> 00:01:07.720
in Far From Home?

00:01:07.720 --> 00:01:10.800
Or are they simply a bold fashion statement
that will earn him lots of mockery from his

00:01:10.800 --> 00:01:11.800
friends?

00:01:11.800 --> 00:01:12.960
Only time will tell.

00:01:13.440 --> 00:01:14.760
"Sup, dickwad."

00:01:15.320 --> 00:01:19.780
Marvel has a history of altering trailer footage
to feed the hype machine, like including Hulk

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:23.600
at the Battle of Wakanda in the Infinity War
spot, or leaving a ton of it on the cutting

00:01:23.600 --> 00:01:28.180
room floor, like Black Widow getting her aggression
out at the firing range in those Endgame trailers.

00:01:28.180 --> 00:01:32.731
The latest Spider-Man: Far From Home trailer
is no exception, with a sneaky Spider Suit

00:01:32.740 --> 00:01:36.240
switcheroo happening between the "Teaser Trailer"
and the "Official Trailer."

00:01:36.240 --> 00:01:41.040
In the Teaser Trailer, Peter is seen sporting
his Homecoming-era suit while making his appearance

00:01:41.040 --> 00:01:44.580
with Aunt May at the Salvation Army's "Homeless
Support" event in NYC.

00:01:44.580 --> 00:01:49.020
Your Friendly Neighborhood Spider-Man is still
outfitted in the iconic red-and-blue backstage,

00:01:49.020 --> 00:01:52.420
minus the mask, when he's caught in the middle
of May and Happy's flirt session.

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:56.940
But in the latest Official Trailer, Peter
is wearing his Iron Spider suit at the event,

00:01:56.940 --> 00:02:00.320
meaning the Teaser Trailer clips were either
shot twice or there's some seamless CGI in

00:02:00.320 --> 00:02:01.320
play.

00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.560
We know it's the same location because of
the recessed lights above the kitchen prep

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:06.140
area in the background.

00:02:06.140 --> 00:02:07.300
So what gives?

00:02:07.300 --> 00:02:11.720
Well, the Iron Spider suit has more significance
for Peter now that the suit's designer, once-reluctant

00:02:11.720 --> 00:02:14.180
father figure Tony Stark, has passed on.

00:02:14.180 --> 00:02:18.760
It's just speculation, but Marvel also probably
didn't want to blatantly spoil Peter's fate

00:02:18.760 --> 00:02:23.130
in Endgame by showing him alive and well wearing
the same suit he disintegrated in at the end

00:02:23.130 --> 00:02:24.140
of Infinity War.

00:02:24.140 --> 00:02:28.540
Regardless, this Loki-level trickery is yet
another example of Marvel going to great lengths

00:02:28.540 --> 00:02:32.680
to hide the details of its MCU blockbusters
in advance of opening day.

00:02:32.700 --> 00:02:37.120
If the Spider-Man origin you remember is the
one from the first, Sam Raimi-directed Spider-Man

00:02:37.120 --> 00:02:38.800
movie, you don't remember Crusher Hogan.

00:02:38.800 --> 00:02:43.720
You remember Macho Man Randy Savage's Bonesaw
McGraw, who likely got that name because Savage

00:02:43.720 --> 00:02:45.860
would never have played a character named
"Hogan."

00:02:45.860 --> 00:02:47.900
Too much bad blood between him and the Hulkster.

00:02:47.900 --> 00:02:51.660
But the wrestler Peter Parker originally took
on in the comics when he was looking for fame

00:02:51.660 --> 00:02:55.970
was indeed named Crusher Hogan, and if you
look closely behind Happy Hogan, no relation,

00:02:55.970 --> 00:03:00.880
you can see a poster advertising Crusher's
original offer: $100 to anyone who can stay

00:03:00.880 --> 00:03:02.540
in the ring with him for three minutes.

00:03:02.540 --> 00:03:06.220
There's also a little bell there, so maybe
this is the building where he issued the challenge.

00:03:06.220 --> 00:03:10.020
We never saw the full origin of Tom Holland's
Spider-Man, but it's entirely possible to

00:03:10.020 --> 00:03:14.300
believe he took on and beat Crusher prior
to the life-changing night his Uncle Ben died.

00:03:14.340 --> 00:03:19.320
In July 2018, Deadline reported that Turkish
actor Numan Acar had taken on the role of

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:21.440
"Dmitri" in Spider-Man: Far From Home.

00:03:21.500 --> 00:03:25.940
The report further theorized that he may be
playing Dmitri Smerdyakov, a half-brother

00:03:25.940 --> 00:03:29.400
of Kraven the Hunter known better to Spider-Man
fans as Chameleon.

00:03:29.400 --> 00:03:34.200
He's one of Spider-Man's oldest rogues, appearing
all the way back in Amazing Spider-Man #1.

00:03:34.200 --> 00:03:35.180
Is he in the trailer?

00:03:35.180 --> 00:03:39.160
It's hard to say, but there are lots of places
he could be, given that Chameleon's whole

00:03:39.160 --> 00:03:42.660
deal is that he can look like anyone, just
like Mystique in the X-Men movies.

00:03:42.660 --> 00:03:46.360
One of the criminals Spider-Man apprehends
in the fancy ballroom early on in the trailer

00:03:46.360 --> 00:03:48.800
is wearing what look like leopard-print pajamas.

00:03:48.800 --> 00:03:52.900
This may be an early Dmitri appearance, wearing
something similar to what his fur-loving relative

00:03:52.900 --> 00:03:53.900
would sport.

00:03:53.920 --> 00:03:57.560
Or he could be throughout the rest of the
trailer, looking like just about anyone.

00:03:57.560 --> 00:03:59.780
We have to assume Mysterio is up to no good.

00:03:59.780 --> 00:04:04.320
Could the Nick Fury or Maria Hill Spider-Man
meets in Italy be Chameleon in disguise, working

00:04:04.320 --> 00:04:06.520
on Mysterio's behalf in some huge ruse?

00:04:06.520 --> 00:04:10.239
They definitely have a lot of reasons in their
back pocket as to why only Spider-Man can

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:11.060
do this job.

00:04:11.060 --> 00:04:12.480
Or heck, he may be MJ.

00:04:12.960 --> 00:04:15.140
"I mean it's kind of obvious."

00:04:15.540 --> 00:04:19.820
While the impacts of Peter and countless others
missing out on five years of life are still

00:04:19.829 --> 00:04:24.150
up in the air, one thing in the second Far
From Home trailer is pretty clear: this new,

00:04:24.150 --> 00:04:26.300
revived world has nothing but love for Iron
Man.

00:04:26.300 --> 00:04:30.200
The trailer starts with Peter looking at a
giant mural of the fallen hero on the side

00:04:30.200 --> 00:04:34.120
of a building in New York City, but that's
far from the only tribute that Tony gets.

00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:37.880
In addition to a memorial that appears to
be somewhere in Europe, viewers can also see

00:04:37.889 --> 00:04:41.910
many drawings of Iron Man in the background
of an art class at Peter's school, showing

00:04:41.910 --> 00:04:46.230
that the world post-Endgame recognizes that
it owes everything, or, well, half of everything,

00:04:46.230 --> 00:04:48.360
to the one, the only, invincible Iron Man.

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:53.160
Tony was a huge part of Peter's origin story
in the MCU, and even in death, he still looms

00:04:53.169 --> 00:04:57.400
large over Peter's day-to-day world, whether
he's out doing hero things or just trying

00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.120
to finish high school after five weird years
away.

00:05:00.280 --> 00:05:04.199
Towards the end of the trailer, Peter can
be seen with a Spider-Man-styled hologram

00:05:04.199 --> 00:05:05.270
over his wrist.

00:05:05.270 --> 00:05:09.220
He reacts to the device with some surprise,
looking offscreen to catch somebody's eye.

00:05:09.220 --> 00:05:12.460
The way the trailer is edited, it appears
he's looking at Happy Hogan.

00:05:12.460 --> 00:05:15.419
It isn't clear exactly where they are, but
they seem to be surrounded by some relatively

00:05:15.419 --> 00:05:18.650
high-tech decor, maybe on board Happy's sick-looking
jet.

00:05:18.650 --> 00:05:22.729
It seems possible that Tony's left at least
one more surprise behind for Peter, with the

00:05:22.729 --> 00:05:27.020
wrist tech seeming to hearken back to a similar,
physical bracelet Peter showed off during

00:05:27.020 --> 00:05:29.840
the end credits stinger of Captain America:
Civil War.

00:05:29.840 --> 00:05:33.879
Alternatively, this could be some sort of
device from the mysterious Quentin Beck, who's

00:05:33.880 --> 00:05:37.480
been known in the comics to use technology
and illusions to present the appearance of

00:05:37.480 --> 00:05:38.480
superpowers.

00:05:38.560 --> 00:05:41.880
The only thing we can tell from Pete's expression
is he's surprised.

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:42.840
Good surprised?

00:05:42.840 --> 00:05:43.780
Bad surprised?

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:44.860
We'll find out soon.

